                        <div id="accordions" class="accordion">
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse1"><span><strong>Q1:</strong> What is included in book formatting services?</span></div></div><div id="collapse1" class="collapse show"><div class="card-body text"><p>Book formatting services include the complete interior layout and typesetting of your manuscript, chapter heading design, font selection, margin and gutter setup, page numbering, running headers, paragraph spacing, and any special elements your book contains like images, tables, footnotes, indexes, or bibliographies. We deliver platform-ready files in every format you need, print-ready PDF, Kindle, ePub, or any combination. Everything is built to the exact specifications of your chosen publishing platform so your files are ready to upload without additional conversion or technical work.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse2"><span><strong>Q2:</strong> Do you format books for both print and eBook platforms?</span></div></div><div id="collapse2" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes, and we format them separately rather than converting one into the other. Print and eBook formatting have fundamentally different technical requirements, print needs fixed page dimensions, precise margins, and carefully controlled page flow, while eBooks need reflowable text, clickable navigation, and compatibility across multiple devices and screen sizes. We create each format individually, built to its specific platform’s standards, so your book looks professional whether a reader is holding a paperback or reading on a Kindle.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse3"><span><strong>Q3:</strong> How long does the formatting process take?</span></div></div><div id="collapse3" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Standard formatting for a straightforward novel or non-fiction manuscript typically takes five to seven business days. More complex projects, children’s picture books, illustrated non-fiction, cookbooks, academic titles with footnotes and indexes, take longer depending on the level of layout work involved. Rush turnarounds are available for urgent publication deadlines, subject to availability. We’ll give you a realistic timeline during your free assessment based on your manuscript specifically, and we always communicate upfront if a deadline is tight.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse4"><span><strong>Q4:</strong> What file format should I submit my manuscript in?</span></div></div><div id="collapse4" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Microsoft Word (.docx) is the preferred format for submission, as it gives us the cleanest starting point for professional formatting. If your manuscript is in another format, Google Docs, Pages, PDF, or plain text, we can work with that too, though Word is ideal. The important thing is that your manuscript is complete, edited, and final before formatting begins. Formatting is the last production step before publishing, changes to the text after formatting require re-typesetting, which adds time and cost.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse5"><span><strong>Q5:</strong> Do you offer revisions after formatting?</span></div></div><div id="collapse5" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes, revisions are included in every formatting project. Once you receive your formatted files, you review them and let us know if anything needs adjusting, font preferences, spacing, heading styles, page breaks, or any other layout detail. We revise until you’re completely satisfied with how your book looks. What isn’t included is rewriting or editing the text itself, content changes after formatting require re-typesetting, so we always recommend finalising your manuscript completely before the formatting stage begins.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse6"><span><strong>Q6:</strong> Is proofreading or editing included in formatting services?</span></div></div><div id="collapse6" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>No, formatting and editing are separate services, and your manuscript should be fully edited and proofread before formatting begins. Formatting takes your finalised text and turns it into a professionally typeset, platform-ready book. If text changes are needed after formatting, pages need to be re-typeset, which adds time and cost. If your manuscript still needs editing or proofreading, we offer both services and can schedule them before formatting so everything happens in the right order.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse7"><span><strong>Q7:</strong> Do you provide support for publishing platforms like Amazon KDP?</span></div></div><div id="collapse7" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes. We format files to the exact specifications of Amazon KDP, IngramSpark, Apple Books, Kobo, Google Play, and every other major publishing platform. Our files are built to pass each platform’s file review without rejection, so you can upload and publish without technical issues. If you need help with the actual upload process, setting up your KDP account, entering metadata, selecting categories, or configuring pricing, we offer publishing support services that cover everything from file upload through to your book going live.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse8"><span><strong>Q8:</strong> How much do book formatting services cost in Melbourne?</span></div></div><div id="collapse8" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Formatting costs depend on your manuscript’s length, complexity, and the number of formats you need. A standard novel formatted for Kindle and paperback costs less than a heavily illustrated children’s book or an academic title with footnotes, tables, and indexes. Most professional formatting services charge per page or per project, with complexity and format count affecting the final price. We don’t quote without seeing your manuscript, get in touch and we’ll give you clear, honest pricing based on your book’s actual requirements.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse9"><span><strong>Q9:</strong> Will my book meet industry publishing standards?</span></div></div><div id="collapse9" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes. Every book we format meets the professional typesetting and technical standards expected by major publishing platforms and print-on-demand services. This includes correct margins and bleed settings for print, properly embedded fonts, industry-standard paragraph and spacing conventions, and platform-compliant file formats for every retailer you’re publishing through. Your book will be indistinguishable from traditionally published titles in terms of interior quality and formatting standards.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse10"><span><strong>Q10:</strong> Can I request a customised layout or design?</span></div></div><div id="collapse10" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Absolutely. While we recommend genre-appropriate layouts based on what works best for your type of book, we’re happy to accommodate specific preferences, custom chapter heading designs, particular font choices, unique page layouts, drop caps, ornamental breaks, and any other design elements you want incorporated into your book’s interior. For heavily designed books like children’s titles, cookbooks, or coffee table books, custom layout work is standard. We’ll discuss your preferences during the planning stage and show you samples before committing to the final design.</p></div></div></div>
